{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/892080-werewolf-the-forsaken-1st-edition-vs-2nd","id":892080,"title":"Werewolf the Forsaken 1st edition vs 2nd?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-16T15:52:25-07:00","id":892080,"title":"Werewolf the Forsaken 1st edition vs 2nd?","content":"Greetings everyone,<br /> <br /> I'm debating on whether or not to pick up 2nd edition. I have a lot of 1st edition books, and I'm hesitant to make them all obsolete. However, the new Pack source book is intriguing! Are there any guidelines to port 1st edition material over to 2e? What are your thoughts on the new rules? Are the new 2e mechanics updates worth it?<br /> <br /> I looked around for an existing thread on the topic and didn't immediately find one, links to existing discussions are welcome.<br /> <br /> I appreciate your thoughts and input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11795-shexara","name":"Shexara","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T16:05:00-07:00","id":892087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shexara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/892080-werewolf-the-forsaken-1st-edition-vs-2nd#post892080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings everyone,<br /> <br /> I'm debating on whether or not to pick up 2nd edition. I have a lot of 1st edition books, and I'm hesitant to make them all obsolete. However, the new Pack source book is intriguing! Are there any guidelines to port 1st edition material over to 2e? What are your thoughts on the new rules? Are the new 2e mechanics updates worth it?<br /> <br /> I looked around for an existing thread on the topic and didn't immediately find one, links to existing discussions are welcome.<br /> <br /> I appreciate your thoughts and input.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I vastly prefer the Gift system Werewolf 2e uses as opposed to 1e's since it's A. More intuitive and B. Easier to select things in. It is far less restrictive and allows for diversity even in a new pack with members who might pick the same theme of gifts as a basis. For instance, a Pack with 2 Iron Masters can have the difference of being more subtle or being more overt with their technology gifts, one has Garble which is mostly a subterfuge and descrete sabotage effect, the other has Unmake which is a powerful destruction of machinery effect. And neither is inherently stronger than the other, just different.<br /> <br /> Once more, there's no issues where some Gift categories have <i>nothing </i>for a werewolf that doesn't have specific Renown focuses. <br /> <br /> However, most Gifts from 1e are unusable with the new system with some exceptions.<br /> The Auspice Gifts in Signs of the Moon are rather easily intergrated with 2e mechanics if you treat them as &quot;Moon Gifts&quot; which is ironically fitting....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 05-16-2016, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T16:08:47-07:00","id":892092,"title":"","content":"I think it's better, most importantly it doesn't invalidate most of the 1e supplements. I made a lot of use of Predators, Tribes of the Moon, and Blood of the Wolf when I started running my 2e game.<br /> <br /> Biggest change to the lore is the centrality of a large pack to the game, and the removal of the unihar. Some like the latter change, some don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T16:19:36-07:00","id":892099,"title":"","content":"I like 2e waaaaaaaaaaaay better! Renown is used for much more now so it feels well worth buying instead of an experience sink you have to deal with to get the Gifts you want with half way decent dice pools. The Gifts system is much more usable and Gifts themselves feel much more thematic for werewolves. The forms all have practical applications for different situations instead of Urshul always being the overall best. Death Rage feels scary instead of just an inconvenience. Harmony is actually about balancing between your dual natures of spirit and flesh instead of a &quot;how well do you follow the Oath of the Moon?&quot; meter. Tribes actually have a distinct role in Werewolf society and culture that doesn't feel redundant with Auspice. Every Rite feels cool, thematic, and powerful for its cost regardless of dot level instead of the low level ones feeling like exp taxes. Wolf-Blooded are actually badass instead of just humans with some bonus dice against Lunacy. Lunacy actually feels relevant. The tweaks to the fluff make it much more intuitive how a character would logically transition from a clueless human into werewolf society. It's just a better game all around and I love it so much. All of this ON TOP OF the improvements 2e makes to the core rules system. I highly recommend it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T17:19:30-07:00","id":892134,"title":"","content":"While there are some specific 1e CofD rules I prefer over the 2e CofD rules (though I think 2e is superior in aggregate), the Werewolf specific rules are vastly superior in 2e. I can't think of a single 1e rule that 2e has covered that isn't superior in application in 2e.<br /> <br /> The big issue I think for people looking at converting isn't going to be the rules. It's the focus of the game more strongly around werewolves as hunters. This focus makes for a very strong game, and in many ways curbstomps a lot of the criticisms about Forsaken being too &quot;bland.&quot; But at times it can feel a bit limiting compared to 1e.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I have trouble seeing anyone that's open to the thematic changes reading 2e and regretting it. I'd say pick up the pdf at least if you can afford it. The worst thing is you only use it to mine for ideas for your 1e games (they don't magically expire if you buy the new book...) because it has a lot of things that are worth considering even if you decide to stick with 1e. On the other end, you find 2e superior and for the most part. It's a lot more complete out of the gate without a need to wait for/port yourself 1e stuff to it (unless you really like having a lot of Lodges in your games, but even then they're not hard to update with The Pack's rules for them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T17:21:37-07:00","id":892137,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for your input! Your enthusiasm makes me want to buy the new books right now. (And I may just do so!) It also makes my heart glad to hear that moving to 2nd edition won't immediately make all of my books useless!<br /> <br /> It looks like like things are now call Chronicles of Darkness. Am I safe to assume that I will need to pick up a &quot;Chronicles of Darkness&quot; book to replace the (new) World of Darkness core book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11795-shexara","name":"Shexara","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T17:27:25-07:00","id":892140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shexara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/892080-werewolf-the-forsaken-1st-edition-vs-2nd?p=892137#post892137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you all for your input! Your enthusiasm makes me want to buy the new books right now. (And I may just do so!) It also makes my heart glad to hear that moving to 2nd edition won't immediately make all of my books useless!<br /> <br /> It looks like like things are now call Chronicles of Darkness. Am I safe to assume that I will need to pick up a &quot;Chronicles of Darkness&quot; book to replace the (new) World of Darkness core book?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not neccesarily. Part of the 2e change over is that all Gamelines now have a copy of the &quot;quick&quot; and essential rules for play within their books. It thus becomes rather easy to play with just WtE 2e alone with some basic applications of common sense for most circumstances... though specific rules are not in the quick notes.<br /> <br /> The main Chronicles book is an expanded version of the rules that goes into significantly higher detail over them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 05-16-2016, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T17:28:12-07:00","id":892141,"title":"","content":"If you are only interested in Werewolf, no. The book is self contained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T23:13:06-07:00","id":892323,"title":"","content":"The new 2e core books have all the core rules in them. What gets truncated depends on the game and its focus. None of the supernatural cores have all of the Merits and subsystems that the CofD core does. So you don't need it, but it remains useful to have despite the overlap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T23:38:31-07:00","id":892332,"title":"","content":"My biggest reason for preferring 2E werewolf is that werewolves can breed with each other without creating a monster. So by the child practically being guaranteed to be a wolf blooded instead of a monster I find it easier to believe that they have both stable bloodlines and not a vast gain amount of humans for breeding out of necessity. I know it wasn't quite presented that way in 1E but it is what i saw as potentially necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T23:49:28-07:00","id":892333,"title":"","content":"Hi, I saw an advertisement about filling a spot on a chorus? Why, of course I know &quot;Werewolf 2e Is So Much Better Than 1e&quot; - it's one of my favorite tunes!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T00:29:55-07:00","id":892351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/892080-werewolf-the-forsaken-1st-edition-vs-2nd?p=892333#post892333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, I saw an advertisement about filling a spot on a chorus? Why, of course I know &amp;quot;Werewolf 2e Is So Much Better Than 1e&amp;quot; - it's one of my favorite tunes!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well opinions were asked so opinions are being given. If you feel one side is too loud offer a counter point to give the under repisented side voice. <br /> <br /> What was better in 1e werewolf? <br /> <br /> My knowledge of first edition werewolf is pretty much that werewolves were forbidden to breed with each other and for good reason. I am not familiar with first edition werewolf so enlighten me on its strengths. I honestly don't know what was changed except that one detail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T00:47:38-07:00","id":892362,"title":"","content":"You're mistaking jovial enthusiasm for sarcasm. I really do very much prefer 2nd edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T07:24:23-07:00","id":892486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/892080-werewolf-the-forsaken-1st-edition-vs-2nd?p=892351#post892351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well opinions were asked so opinions are being given. If you feel one side is too loud offer a counter point to give the under repisented side voice.<br /> <br /> What was better in 1e werewolf?<br /> <br /> My knowledge of first edition werewolf is pretty much that werewolves were forbidden to breed with each other and for good reason. I am not familiar with first edition werewolf so enlighten me on its strengths. I honestly don't know what was changed except that one detail.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Main diferences over 1st and 2nd:<br /> If you are familiar with 2nd ed I will tell you bout the 1st<br /> <br /> They could not breed because they consider each other like brothers and sisters and incest is .. wierd.. Just like humans.. when cousins have sons they are born retarded. (here they are born spiritual monsters)<br /> In 1st Ed the idea of Pack was short-sighted, the whole thing of humans and wolves in the pack was a big doubt if it could or could not. (Wolf-blooded was already on it but it was useless for the most part. It was just there for fluff)<br /> <br /> Gauru form was more limited, you had to roll a dice-pool and play as gauru for only some turns determined by the amount of success. <br /> Kuruth in 2nd edition system is both an advantage and disadvantage. In 1st It was only problems and there was no criterion to tell what to do during kuruth both for GM or Player. The Only criterion were that you are fucked during a time determined by your primal-urge.<br /> <br /> Things that I dislike in 2nd edition concerns antagonists: <br /> I've already didnt know what to motive my players in 1st edition because the enemies was not so emphasized. But at least they were there.<br /> <br /> The Pure. What the hell happen here? if you never read about then you couldnt care less.<br /> The Host. How to use then, how to make a good game with then?NOthing (but there are good tales between chapters)<br /> Bale Hounds There are two phrases saying something about it. I was expecting way more for then as the 9th tribe.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T08:50:44-07:00","id":892551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/892080-werewolf-the-forsaken-1st-edition-vs-2nd?p=892486#post892486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">when cousins have sons they are born retarded.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">This right here is a serious rule 1 violation. Since you're new here I'm just going to give you a warning, but this would normally earn you a week long suspension.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T15:58:04-07:00","id":892845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/892080-werewolf-the-forsaken-1st-edition-vs-2nd?p=892486#post892486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Main diferences over 1st and 2nd:<br /> If you are familiar with 2nd ed I will tell you bout the 1st<br /> <br /> They could not breed because they consider each other like brothers and sisters and incest is .. wierd.. Just like humans.. <b>1)when cousins have sons they are born retarded</b>. (here they are born spiritual monsters)<br /> In 1st Ed the idea of Pack was short-sighted, the whole thing of humans and wolves in the pack was a<b> 2)</b> <b>big doubt if it could or could not.</b> (Wolf-blooded was already on it but it was useless for the most part. It was just there for fluff)<br /> <br /> Gauru form was more limited, <b>3)you had to roll a dice-pool and play as gauru for only some turns determined by the amount of success.</b><br /> Kuruth in 2nd edition system is both an advantage and disadvantage. In 1st It was only problems and there was no criterion to tell what to do during kuruth both for GM or Player. The Only criterion were that you are fucked during a time determined by your primal-urge.<br /> <br /> Things that I dislike in 2nd edition concerns antagonists:<br /> I've already didnt know what to motive my players in 1st edition because the enemies was not so emphasized. But at least they were there.<br /> <br /> The Pure. What the hell happen here? if you never read about then you couldnt care less.<br /> The Host. How to use then, how to make a good game with then?NOthing (but there are good tales between chapters)<br /> <b>4)Bale Hounds There are two phrases saying something about it. I was expecting way more for then as the 9th tribe.</b></div> </div> </div> </div> \u200b1) Not factually correct. Also offensively worded as pointed out by Charlaquin.<br /> <br /> 2) No doubt, they could not be pack members, neither could wolf blooded unless/until they became full Uratha. They could support a pack but not be true members of one.<br /> <br /> 3) Nope, not correct. Primal Urge plus Stamina rounds determined how long you could safely assume Gauru. You Auspice renown was added if your Auspice moon was in the sky. If you failed to make a shifting roll or spend a point of Essence you were automatically dropped down into human form. The only way to increase this duration was to give in to Death Rage and go berserk which meant you temporarily lost control over your character's actions and attacked whatever was closest to you, hopefully not someone you gave a crap about. The book told you what happened during Death Rage. This is all on page 171 of the core rule book.<br /> <br /> 4) They aren't the 9th Tribe unless you use that as an option from Blasphemies, it was never something covered in the main core book. Don't criticize one edition over another because the newer edition doesn't have the supplemental material the first one did. Same goes for the Pure and Hosts. I'm very much looking forward to seeing them all properly covered eventually and hope to see that sooner rather than later.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T17:02:04-07:00","id":892876,"title":"","content":"The second edition does suffer from a over reliance in Idigams (carried from it's earliest incarnation as the Idigam Chronicles). Out of context antagonists that sorta leave you wondering why put so much emphasis on tribal favored prey when they're discussed minimally.<br /> <br /> 32 pages of word count devoted to them, in fact. Could have done away with maybe 2 less of those, maybe dedicate 10 pages to the other, y'know, more common antagonists. Hell, maybe have introduced some lodges.<br /> <br /> Crying over spilled milk, anyhow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T18:07:58-07:00","id":892897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/892080-werewolf-the-forsaken-1st-edition-vs-2nd?p=892876#post892876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second edition does suffer from a over reliance in Idigams (carried from it's earliest incarnation as the Idigam Chronicles). Out of context antagonists that sorta leave you wondering why put so much emphasis on tribal favored prey when they're discussed minimally.<br /> <br /> 32 pages of word count devoted to them, in fact. Could have done away with maybe 2 less of those, maybe dedicate 10 pages to the other, y'know, more common antagonists. Hell, maybe have introduced some lodges.<br /> <br /> Crying over spilled milk, anyhow.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWith the exception of the bit about Lodges I pretty much agree with this. Alternately, I would have preferred some of the Hunting Grounds word count being dedicated instead to the Hosts and Pure (with maybe some Lodge info thrown in). I just don't have the use for those write-ups that others may have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T19:45:59-07:00","id":892956,"title":"","content":"I would however, point out that this seems more of a problem with second edition in general than a problem specific to Werewolf's second edition. There is a fairly large assumption that if you pick up a 2E book, you're familiar with 1E and the background and antagonists found there. Strix get a lot more word count than say Seven and in Werewolf Idigam get a lot more word count than say Bale Hounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T20:03:21-07:00","id":892965,"title":"","content":"Mind, those two antagonist groups needed to be specifically tailored/designed by the ST back in 1e.<br /> <br /> And Forsaken lives and dies by it's antagonists. In Requiem the dance macabre, the politics and the building grudges and feuds take the cake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T20:07:48-07:00","id":892971,"title":"","content":"Oh, I'm not griping that its horrible or anything, as a lover of 1E, I also have a great amount of love for 2E. I can just understand that if you're a new player, its going to be pretty difficult to see and understand what makes an Abyssal different from a Corruption Spirit etc. I just used the above examples because they were the quickest I could think of. I'm happy to wait for some more books, I can just understand a new player not really getting Azlu and Beshilu etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T01:50:44-07:00","id":893152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/892080-werewolf-the-forsaken-1st-edition-vs-2nd?p=892876#post892876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second edition does suffer from a over reliance in Idigams (carried from it's earliest incarnation as the Idigam Chronicles). Out of context antagonists that sorta leave you wondering why put so much emphasis on tribal favored prey when they're discussed minimally.<br /> <br /> 32 pages of word count devoted to them, in fact. Could have done away with maybe 2 less of those, maybe dedicate 10 pages to the other, y'know, more common antagonists. Hell, maybe have introduced some lodges.<br /> <br /> Crying over spilled milk, anyhow.</div> </div> </div> </div>From memory, it was long after final drafts were submitted that the decision was taken that it was now officially a Second Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T01:55:14-07:00","id":893154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/892080-werewolf-the-forsaken-1st-edition-vs-2nd?p=892486#post892486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bale Hounds There are two phrases saying something about it. I was expecting way more for then as the 9th tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Darksider said above, Bale Hounds as a 9th tribe was never locked in a definitive. It was one of several options for STs to use what they wanted. <br /> <br /> Presenting them as such was always unlikely in the core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T04:15:21-07:00","id":893198,"title":"","content":"Bale Hounds are mentioned twice in the Forsaken core book. Ironically, neither in a section that actually explains what the Bale Hounds are. One is the Idigiam section, where investigations into the Endless end up pointing to the &quot;Pure or Bale Hounds&quot; instead of something else. No mention of what Bale Hounds look like, do, etc. The second mention is in the Holmes County, Ohio setting blurb. There's mention of Bale Hound trailer park in Charm in the Prey section, but curiously enough? In the Predator section that actually talks about the werewolves in the area? &quot;Transient werewolves&quot; is pretty much the only description there. No mention of a Wound, just brutal murders. <br /> <br /> While I'm not going to say that Bale Hounds don't exist, it feels like they, and the Maeljin, play a far smaller role in 2e than 1e to the point of being all but ignored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T04:37:34-07:00","id":893204,"title":"","content":"I actually have no idea what a bale hound even is since I only have werewolf 2e edition and no 1e books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T05:00:20-07:00","id":893207,"title":"","content":"Someone else can probably explain it better than myself, but if memory serves, the Bale Hounds are werewolves who basically decide that they're going to throw in their lot with extremely nasty spirits called Maeljin who are representative of the seven deadly sins. This corrupts them both inside and out and their preferred tactics are to pretend to be werewolves of other tribes, infiltrate packs and then tempt them into the sin they joined up with. Hoping to corrupt their targets and make them fall as they had. They also spend some of their spare time creating and strengthening Wounds. Wounds being areas in the Shadow which have become infected with corruption and evil that then begin influencing the area around them to fall to similar corruption. For example, a wound of wrath caused by a murder will create nasty murder spirits that will likely use their influence on the material world to cause more murders, spreading the infamy of murders in the region and making the wound larger and more powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T05:14:26-07:00","id":893210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/892080-werewolf-the-forsaken-1st-edition-vs-2nd?p=893204#post893204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually have no idea what a bale hound even is since I only have werewolf 2e edition and no 1e books.</div> </div> </div> </div> Basically this - back in 1e, there were the Maeljin - embodiments of nine different Vices (violence, deception, plus the seven usual). Turns out, these were Infernal demons poking their head into the world through Wounds and infecting regular spirits with demonic energies. <br /> <br /> Bale Hounds were basically werewolves who agreed to align themselves with one of these nine demon lords instead of a Tribal Totem and did evil things in exchange for... umm... dunno, the usual demon's bargain type stituation. <br /> <br /> Cue to 2e, where the Vices have become less of a thing. Its so less of a thing to the point we don't even have Vices in several games, and you can take things like Cautious / Loving as your Virtue / Vices in others. I don't know if this is just a thing were the Inferno is going away, or because its becoming its own game line, or what. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T06:09:16-07:00","id":893232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/892080-werewolf-the-forsaken-1st-edition-vs-2nd?p=893210#post893210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Cue to 2e, where the Vices have become less of a thing. Its so less of a thing to the point we don't even have Vices in several games, and you can take things like Cautious / Loving as your Virtue / Vices in others. I don't know if this is just a thing were the Inferno is going away, or because its becoming its own game line, or what.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, this is also the thing. Vices are very different in CoD/Second Editions than they were in NWoD/First Edition. When the Bale Hounds get some dedicated word count, we'll have to examine what the Maeljin even are these days, in CoD terms.<br /> <br /> As for what Bale Hounds are - basically corrupted werewolves. Some people love them for the 'enemy within' vibe and games centred around that. Personally, I'm less enamoured because I have another half-dozen game lines I can play if I want conspiracy enemy within settings. (This doesn't mean that I don't like Bale Hounds, just that I much prefer my werewolves hunting their prey and dealing with threats that are both bigger and more alien than they are, rather than werewolves gone to the dark side.)<br /> <br /> YMMV, of course.<br /> <br /> There's an awesome thread <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds\">here</a> where various posters spoke what they liked about Bale Hounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T08:39:09-07:00","id":893341,"title":"","content":"Bale Hounds are to the Forsaken and Pure as Scelesti are to the Pentacle and Seers of the Throne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T08:46:43-07:00","id":893349,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Scelesti are a good analogy there. With the concept of the Maeladar, the idea that you will become an immortal Maeltinet, there's a bit of the Seers in them. The Maeljin, as corrupt as they are, are understandable and appreciable on the level that the Exarchs are. Sin and Tyranny have been explored throughout the human experience. What the Abyss is and offers is something alien.<br /> <br /> They can work on the same level as infiltrators, but they can also be outside antagonists like the Seers, depending on which option you go with them.<br /> <br /> It's probably worth keeping in mind that they're still werewolves, and still hunt.<br /> <br /> Either way, I'd suggest going with second edition. The system is better and you can convert first edition stuff over for things that haven't been updated yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-18-2016, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T12:55:53-07:00","id":893529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/892080-werewolf-the-forsaken-1st-edition-vs-2nd?p=893152#post893152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From memory, it was long after final drafts were submitted that the decision was taken that it was now officially a Second Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I acknowledged that in my first line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T18:50:29-07:00","id":893782,"title":"","content":"I'm convinced. 2nd edition book ordered! Thanks again!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"li